Fully automated pipeline deployment.

#                 CHAPTER 4 - The Future of Config Driven Workflows
Advanced features that push the boundaries of what declarative DAG development can achieve

# Beyond Basic DAGs: Advanced Features

1. Custom Operators - 
Reference and configure your own custom Airflow operators directly within YAML definitions. No need to modify Python factory code for each new operator type.
Organizations build custom operators for:
  internal APIs
  proprietary systems
  company tools

2. Callbacks - 
Specify on_success_callback and on_failure_callback functions per task or DAG, enabling rich alerting and monitoring without boilerplate Python.
  Example:
    Send Slack alert
    Send email
    Trigger incident ticket
  
3. KubernetesPodOperator
Very important in modern cloud Airflow.
Each task runs inside isolated Kubernetes pod.
YAML can define:
  Docker image
  CPU
  memory
  environment variables

4. Datasets & Modern Scheduling
Airflow 2.4 introduced data-aware scheduling. Define dataset dependencies and event-driven triggers declaratively 
within your YAML configurations.
Old scheduling:
  Run every day at 6 AM
Modern scheduling:
  Run when upstream dataset updates

